   "ts": "1772438700.000000",
   "channel_id": "C0LTTOOL",
   "user_id": "U0LTFA",
   "text": "T-11 (self-service standardisation) went live this morning with the residential self-service portal. Details are on the instance configuration page in DESKADM.",
   "thread_ts": null,
   "reply_count": 0,
   "reactions": []
  },
  {
   "ts": "1772439600.000001",
   "channel_id": "C0LTTOOL",
   "user_id": "U0LTPS",
   "text": "Does that change anything for us on the front line?",
   "thread_ts": null,
   "reply_count": 0,
   "reactions": []
  },
  {
   "ts": "1772439840.000002",
   "channel_id": "C0LTTOOL",
   "user_id": "U0LTFA",
   "text": "Not for logging - keep categorising to the guide. The config page has the detail.",
   "thread_ts": null,
   "reply_count": 0,
   "reactions": []
  },
  {
   "ts": "1781631000.000003",
   "channel_id": "C0LTTOOL",
   "user_id": "U0LTFA",
   "text": "Product tag migration finished: every product tag now has its prod_ name from the Q4 catalogue. Old tags stay on closed tickets; recategorise open ones as you touch them.",
   "thread_ts": null,
   "reply_count": 0,
   "reactions": []
  },
  {
   "ts": "1790932200.000004",
   "channel_id": "C0LTTOOL",
   "user_id": "U0LTFA",
   "text": "Monthly admin digest is out (mail). Main change: T-14 CSAT wording and the outage holding macro.",
   "thread_ts": null,
   "reply_count": 0,
   "reactions": []
  },
  {
   "ts": "1794816120.000005",
   "channel_id": "C0LTTOOL",
   "user_id": "U0LTJO",
   "text": "WK-04 tickets are flooding in - is there a macro for the holding reply?",
   "thread_ts": null,
   "reply_count": 0,
   "reactions": []
  },
  {
   "ts": "1794816360.000006",
   "channel_id": "C0LTTOOL",
   "user_id": "U0LTFA",
   "text": "Yes, 'Outage - holding (internal)'. Internal note only, the customer SMS goes from the NOC.",
   "thread_ts": null,
   "reply_count": 0,
   "reactions": []
  },
  {
   "ts": "1794847200.000007",
   "channel_id": "C0LTDQ",
   "user_id": "U0LTMT",
   "text": "W46 audit done: 28 tickets flagged for the 2026-11-18 batch, they're in the Desk Quality base (Audit flags).",
   "thread_ts": null,
   "reply_count": 0,
   "reactions": []
  },
  {
   "ts": "1794928200.000008",
   "channel_id": "C0LTDQ",
   "user_id": "U0LTTR",
   "text": "I've had a first go at all 28 - draft's in the shared folder (recat-draft-trenwick). Mostly type fixes and the new product tags; PA customers bumped to High per 5.3.",
   "thread_ts": null,
   "reply_count": 0,
   "reactions": []
  },
  {
   "ts": "1794929520.000009",
   "channel_id": "C0LTDQ",
   "user_id": "U0LTCL",
   "text": "From Tobias's draft that's 10 questions landing on the self-service worklist after the batch - we'll staff Thursday for 10.",
   "thread_ts": null,
   "reply_count": 0,
   "reactions": []
  },
  {
   "ts": "1794931320.000010",
   "channel_id": "C0LTDQ",
   "user_id": "U0LTMT",
   "text": "Thanks both. The draft is Tobias's working, not the record - the batch goes to the guide. Note under Queue health notes as usual.",
   "thread_ts": null,
   "reply_count": 0,
   "reactions": []
  },
  {
   "ts": "1794929700.000011",
   "channel_id": "C0LTSS",
   "user_id": "U0LTCL",
   "text": "Heads-up team: expecting ~10 residential and business enquiries from the Desk Quality batch on Thursday.",
   "thread_ts": null,
   "reply_count": 0,
   "reactions": []
  },
  {
